{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod","id":1033861,"title":"History lessons - how to fit everything in the cWoD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-17T20:27:00-08:00","id":1033861,"title":"History lessons - how to fit everything in the cWoD","content":"The Impergium, the great flood, the first and second citties, the Fae war of the courts, the sundering of changelling, the great Maelstroms, the Rage wars, the anarchist revolt, the advent of reason, the rise of the Consensus, the creation of the Camarilla and Sabbatt, the birth of the Tremere and Giovanni, the council of the 9 Traditions, the rise of the Technocratic Union, the Inquisition, the destruction of Charon, the destruction of the Bunyup... How can anyone mix all this toghether?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T23:55:09-08:00","id":1033904,"title":"","content":"To really make it all mix together? Fairly, without any gameline getting majorly shafted?<br /> Next to impossible. People have been trying for a long time.<br /> <br /> The world's origin stories of the gamelines clash, the metaphysics of the gameworlds clash, the hidden reasons behind political events clash, who actually controls the world's economy clash. To make it all mesh together, you'd have to compromise and tweak In each case and event and go 'in this case gameline X is right as it works better, perhaps with adjustments for gameline Y and Z'.<br /> <br /> I think the only gamelines that mainly avoid issues are Changeling and Wraith, on account of Changeling not having big global events (aside of the Fae leaving), and Wraith being its own thing mostly containted in the Low Umbra/Shadowlands.<br /> <br /> Several of the WoD storyteller books give simple but effective advice:<br /> &quot;If you are playing a gameline X game, treat gameline X as correct and primary. Use gameline Y's stuff if you want, as long as it doesn't conflict&quot;<br /> <br /> The only gameline that officially tried to merge the world origin stories is Demon, and it basically did it by saying 'All the different views were wrong and just an aspect of the same thing happening, but <i>clearly only the Demons</i> know the objective truth.'. Which pretty much was the equivalent of shafting all the other gameline's origin stories' actual importance and truth. Heh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 01-18-2017, 03:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T10:12:13-08:00","id":1034100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1033904#post1033904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The only gameline that officially tried to merge the world origin stories is Demon, and it basically did it by saying 'All the different views were wrong and just an aspect of the same thing happening, but <i>clearly only the Demons</i> know the objective truth.'. Which pretty much was the equivalent of shafting all the other gameline's origin stories' actual importance and truth. Heh.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair (which people seldom are when Demon seems to be trodding on their pet mythology), Demon did state unequivocally that the Demons themselves were unreliable witnesses. The world wasn't at all what it was when they were thrown into the Abyss. It didn't even vaguely function the way it does now. And they are trying to remember it with their memories all mixed up in a limited meat brain in this new and limited world. So, though they can remember that it was different, they themselves aren't even really capable of comprehending what those differences were except by imperfect analogy (and a lot of nostalgia and various other mixed up emotive states). <br /> <br /> It's like they were three dimensional and now they are two (like everyone else) and they are trying to imagine what &quot;depth/height&quot; was like and then trying to remember events that happened at various &quot;heights&quot; all mapped out flat. Oh, and now there's no color. And the vectors are squashed. And time is linear and unidirectional. And meaning and substance aren't related. Cause and effect are related in a very boring way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T13:13:34-08:00","id":1034204,"title":"","content":"Not to forget that all lines can also be equally wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T13:57:15-08:00","id":1034227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1034204#post1034204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to forget that all lines can also be equally wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>But how would you grade what parts score for right or wrong unless you had a definite aim for what the resulting crossover-o-rama was going to look like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T18:06:36-08:00","id":1034365,"title":"","content":"Paradoxically, the gameline in most agreement with the scientific concensus is WTA, as some of the Rokea are old enough to remember the dinosaurs (Rokea are immortal and are really good at surviving). After the fall of the Second City, WtA and VtM concur on dates, which suggests that the Antediluvian Kindred may be refugees from the Astral Umbra.<br /> <br /> If that was the case, Caine would be an Incarna created by the Godhead of the Astral Umbra to represent the concept of Betrayal who figured out how to become something else. He created the 2nd and 3rd Generation within his Astral Realm and kicked out the 3rd Generation when they killed the 2nd Generation. The 3rd Generation possessed mortals and transformed them into the first Kindred (which would make Kindred strangely like the Changeling interpretation of their origin). It would also explain some of the Mage confusion with the nature of the Kindred and why Risen can learn some Kindred Disciplines (Risen being similar to the first Kindred).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T19:13:43-08:00","id":1034404,"title":"","content":"My advice?<br /> <br /> First: give up the notion of one convenient, unified timeline and the &quot;this is how things happened and that was how the world was created&quot; approach of other rpgs and worlds.<br /> <br /> Second: base things on the fact that people are fallible. Memories are fallible, even the memories of beings like methuselahs and mokol\u00e9. Oral tradition is <i>extremely </i>fallible. That that garou say something doesn't make it true, it's a <i>myth</i>. Just because something is in a written source, like the Book of Nod doesn't make it true either, just like in real life. Oh, people are whining about Demon, but honestly, demons don't have the truth either. <i>Their </i>God could have been a lot of things. Just because a game was based on Judeo-Christian mythology and another on animistic faith systems doesn't necessiate that either of them have to be exclusively true. <br /> <br /> IMO, when you embrace that no one has the ultimate truth, just their specific mythos, suddenly the &quot;incompatible&quot; worldviews and creation stories start to matter much less. Accidentally that's how the real world works. Different people and religions have very different ideas about how creation works and how it came to exist.<br /> <br /> In my book the different critters having different stories don't deride the game, on the contrary, it adds to it.<br /> <br /> Going back to history: to me, everything earlier than the high middle ages is <i>extremely </i>fragmented, just like in real life. Rome, we know a bit more about, but that's it. Individuals from those ages, like methuselahs usually aren't willing to give up their knowledge, but if they are, they are still <i>individuals </i>and they can't remember something that didn't happen with them personally in an age before fast travel and communication. Even the antediluvians and <i>even Caine</i> are just persons.<br /> <br /> Or, to put it differently, what a rokea would remeber? Swimming, swimming, swimming. A Plesiosaurus here, an early whale there. Bajilion of fish. More swimming. A tasty seal from not so long ago. History tends to not happening in the deep oceans.<br /> <br /> Everything before the great ancient civilizations is basically a myth and no one knows.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T19:34:35-08:00","id":1034412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1034404#post1034404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, to put it differently, what a rokea would remeber? Swimming, swimming, swimming. A Plesiosaurus here, an early whale there. Bajilion of fish. More swimming. A tasty seal from not so long ago. History tends to not happening in the deep oceans.<br /> <br /> Everything before the great ancient civilizations is basically a myth and no one knows.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lol, that was really funny. I think I just found the most boring and bored critters of WoD haha","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T19:38:45-08:00","id":1034413,"title":"","content":"Some crossover metaplot is VERY problematic thou, because it need really big extrapolations. I guess, imho, that the worse of all is the Union of the Technocratic Conventions, or the Technocracy. Oh, boy, were should we begin...<br /> <br /> Ok, lets do this. In Mage, the Union is almost omnipresent and omnipowerful","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T20:04:06-08:00","id":1034421,"title":"","content":"And that's the thing about the Technocracy. It only makes any sense if they truly control the world. Thats how this group were designed... It loses it's meaning if it is just a bunch of technomancers with limited meaning struggling for power against equal rivals. The Union only makes sense as being the supernaturals cops, and all transgressors are supose to need to work below its radar or risking get caught. Its like the police vs mobs; there will always be gangsters in the world, but they need to be able to work at low profile, they dont get free reign to operate fully in the open.<br /> <br /> Those assumptions, however, are far from the truth in ANY other game.<br /> <br /> How often have a Vampire story ever told about an Elder captured by an spaceship from another dimension?<br /> In Mage, the Order of Reason began a cleasing of the world during middle ages. Sorcerous and witches, demons, crazy beings from the Beyond... All would have to hide or die. Well, you could link that to the Shatering in CtD and the rise of banality, ok... But in Vampire, the Camarilla is created about the same period as a protection against the very mundane Inquisition.... How disappointing.<br /> You COULD make a leap of faith here and say that this mundane Inquisition were just a cover for a bigger Order of Reason conspiration. That's fine by me. Oh, and lets not forget the crucial point were both world collide (violently): the rise of the Tremere clan.<br /> <br /> The Tremere are the beloved ones of the writers of VtM, that is evident everywhere. Fighting the mighty Tzimisce, they found time to capture gangrels and nosferatus, create an entire new bloodline that is perhaps the most peculiar of all, fight all the houses of the Order of Hermes, and climb the generation ladder of the kindred up to the top, and at the same time creating the most specific and versatile of the vampiric powers. All that in their first centuries as neonates. And if thats not enough, they hunted an entire clan to extinction, meanwhile managing to create important connections amongst the kindred that allowed them to became of the the founders and big shots of the Camarilla. Beyond any doubt, they are White Wolf little beloved ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T20:16:13-08:00","id":1034423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1034412#post1034412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lol, that was really funny. I think I just found the most boring and bored critters of WoD haha</div> </div> </div> </div>What I read about them indicates this. Before the underwater nuclear bomb experiments, they didn't do an awfully lot with the surface world. It just didn't bother them. Moreover, their reason of being is <i>survival</i>. That's a bit contradictory with going out to the surface and doing things and meddling with others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ok, lets do this. In Mage, the Union is almost omnipresent and omnipowerful </div> </div> </div>It depends on which version do you use and how much do you want to ST them as that. In recent books, like the revised era, M20 and the new convention books they aren1t so much like that. They like to picture themselves as such and sure, the Traditions are also buying into the omnipresent enemy thing, because that's easier to rally against. But according the books I read (and I admit I didn't read a lot of 1e-2e books yet) they really aren't that way. They have very limited resources, most importantly in the manpower side of things. They're sretching <i>very </i>thin, because there's a very limited number of people awakening in a given time and they have only a portion of them. Yes, they have fingers in a lot of pies and they have access to a lot of things, like government institutions and law enforcement but they can't survey everything constantly and you don't want to share inner things with the sleeper subordinates, or send said subordinates against supernatural threats. Yes, if you are making noise and bring attention on yourself and becoming a major problem, they could strike with a lot of concentrated force, but normally they can't monitor everything an be everywhere.<br /> <br /> Or look at it that way: if they were really omnipresent and omnipowerfull, they'd have eradicated the traditions and every other supernatural critters a long time ago. But they didn't, because they can't.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I don't agree with you conclusion that they make sense only as an omnipresent thing. Yes they're powerful, but they aren't the only ones. They don't clash with the Camarilla, or the Pentex in all-out war, because in reality, you go to war, if you have a reasonably good chance to win without too much loss knowing if you lose too much, a laughing third party would saunter in and swipe the floor with you. That, and Vampires tend to be minding their own business and stay out of the way. Until they don't and then, you'd need to bring out the bombs and sun-lasers. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Being the most powerful group in any given game doesn't necessiate in my book that they must control everything. Yes, they likely the biggest dog in WoD, but don't think in absolutes, they're other not much smaller dogs. They could be menacing, extremely powerful and dangerous without invalidating every other group, IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 01-18-2017, 11:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T20:20:04-08:00","id":1034424,"title":"","content":"But why did the little Tremere crossed the tzimisce road?<br /> <br /> Well, first of all, the Tremere were MAGES. Not sorcerous, not stage tricksters. They were Awakened.<br /> <br /> But not just anyone: they were of the founding houses of the Hermetic Order. Very specific.<br /> <br /> So, why did Tremere decided to become a Vampire?<br /> <br /> Well... He felt &quot;a disturbance in the force&quot;. He predicted that his imortal alchemical drugs would stop working, after centuries of using them just fine, thanks.<br /> <br /> But... WHY? Why would they stop working out of the blue?<br /> <br /> Because of the SCOURGE (PARADOX). Basically, Tremere divinated a world were mages wouldn't be able to get away with massing with the reality any more.<br /> <br /> But... What's the orign of the Scourge?<br /> <br /> It comes from the Consensus.<br /> <br /> Thing is, the Consensus were the thing that the Order of Reason were creating. No Order of Reason, no Consensus, no Scourge, no Tremere vampires. Simple.<br /> <br /> And we can't just remove the Tremere from VtM, that would mess things up... No Tremere, the Salubri are back, no anarchist revolt, no Camarilla, no Sabbat (Im now pretty sure that all of that must be the work of an Entropy m\u00e1ster... Just picture the image of an Entropy 5 effect on Tremere that made him &quot;imagine a world with no magik. Funny idea).<br /> <br /> So, the Order of Reason is a NECESSITY for VtM... Even if all that chain of events is invisible to ALL kindred","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T20:29:35-08:00","id":1034426,"title":"","content":"The thing is... How many times have the Order of Reason or its child the Technocracy EVER dealt with the kindred?<br /> <br /> Well, you'll hear talks (mostly by the side of the Union) about &quot;dealing with those deviants&quot; or using as subjects on their Labs. But THAT'S IT.<br /> <br /> That is, until the Union nuked the Ravnos third generation and pratically summoning the Sun on him while he were having a small heated discussion with 5 kuei jin titans.<br /> <br /> What???","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T20:42:22-08:00","id":1034430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod#post1033861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Impergium, the great flood, the first and second citties, the Fae war of the courts, the sundering of changelling, the great Maelstroms, the Rage wars, the anarchist revolt, the advent of reason, the rise of the Consensus, the creation of the Camarilla and Sabbatt, the birth of the Tremere and Giovanni, the council of the 9 Traditions, the rise of the Technocratic Union, the Inquisition, the destruction of Charon, the destruction of the Bunyup... How can anyone mix all this toghether?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lean into the subjective reality bits and assume Werewolves and Vampires (for example) have interacted with different paradigms of ancient history (to use Mage terminology) - one long involving geological epochs, the other relatively short and Creationist. Demon reinforces this idea with its description of how the world was more &quot;layered&quot; in the pst, and something that takes millions of years on one layer can occur in six days on another.<br /> <br /> The layers interact and continuous events are reflected between them. If we use the idea from &quot;Ascension&quot; of Ixion being the first kinslayer as the first act of magic, and obviously think of this in terms of Cain as well - that makes the Curse of Caine the first Paradox, which may explain why Awakened Magic can't permanently cure it (at least without Telos, the 10th sphere, which was severed from the world by that first murder).<br /> <br /> If we then think of cain slaying Abel as a metaphor for the Neolithic agricultural revolution (Cain was a farmer, Abel a herder like the nomads the farming societies supplanted in the ancient Middle East) - then this also makes sense as the Weaver capturing the Balance Wyrm in its webs, breaking the cycle of humans obeying the natural cycle of resources and instead starting to build settled civilization by making resources grow to fit their population. The loss of Telos and fall of the Balance Wyrm fit together nicely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T20:43:51-08:00","id":1034432,"title":"","content":"And it gets even worse for other games... For example, the Pentex, probably the greatest enemy of ALL the shapeshifters, is part of the Union. A small part of it, to be honest. The entire Pentex is inside the Division Q, a Methodology of the Syndicate. Ok, lets give it some guessed numbers to try to understand: the Syndicate is one out if 5 conventions. Perhaps, Division Q of the Syndicate answers for about one fifth of the entire Syndicate. And Pentex is half of that Methodology. So, 5 x 5 x 2 = 50. That means that the feared organization of the Wyrm answers for only 1/50 of the amount of the power of the Union.<br /> <br /> That's fine, the Union is supposed to be &quot;The Big Brother&quot;. That's it's core concept. So, when you say that half of the Fera's enemies are just a fraction of the bulk of the power of the Union, it fits the concept of an all knowing, all powerful secret conspiration.<br /> <br /> But... How many Garou EVER were gunned down by furious Hit Marks? How many KNOW Caerns were ever sanitized by the VE Qui La Machinae? How many know allied totem spirits of the Garou were EVER destroyed by starships?<br /> <br /> The games intermingle at very important pivotal moments (like the Tremere, the death of Ravnos, the Pentex), but other than those, is as if they never relate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T20:58:51-08:00","id":1034437,"title":"","content":"Now, forgive me, but I think you're exaggerating things.<br /> <br /> The consensus shifting wasn't only the working of the OoR. They played a part in it, a notably big part yes, but they weren't the only reason. <br /> <br /> The events in Vampire history weren't the result of the existence of the Tremere, nor the born of the sects.<br /> <br /> The Tremere could go against the Tzimisce, because that was before the existence of big organizations and the Tzimisce were extremely scattered, they didn't wage war as one. On the other hand, The Tremere were highly organized, they were basically a militant group even before their vampirism.<br /> <br /> About the Technos dealing with Vampires: I'm pretty sure they put out the occasional silly one who's causing a lot of trouble, but Vampires, as I said are very good at regulate themselves. Their whole culture is based on hiding. Moreover the Union have other fish to fry. Oh, yes, they'd <i>love</i> to eradicate those bloodsuckers, on principle. They might even succeed. But they not without losing too much in the process and exposing their backs to the Traditions, Werewolves and other groups.<br /> <br /> And most importantly: the Vampire are just don't the focus of Mage. I'm a fan of crossover and sure, if you're going to do a crossover game and want to use both frequently, there'd be more skirmishes between the two and manipulation, espionage, etc. I'm on the firm opinion that it's doable perfectly. Maybe, with the WWP's plans of uniting the WoD into &quot;One World&quot; wo'd see more stories, modules, setting books and whatnot like that. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T21:03:46-08:00","id":1034440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1034432#post1034432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it gets even worse for other games... For example, the Pentex, probably the greatest enemy of ALL the shapeshifters, is part of the Union. A small part of it, to be honest. The entire Pentex is inside the Division Q, a Methodology of the Syndicate. Ok, lets give it some guessed numbers to try to understand: the Syndicate is one out if 5 conventions. Perhaps, Division Q of the Syndicate answers for about one fifth of the entire Syndicate. And Pentex is half of that Methodology. So, 5 x 5 x 2 = 50. That means that the feared organization of the Wyrm answers for only 1/50 of the amount of the power of the Union.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, but where that even came from???<br /> <br /> As far as I know, the Pentex is most certainly not the part of the Union. There might be mutual projects and occasional alliances, but in the big picture they're more rivals than friends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T21:17:10-08:00","id":1034446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1034423#post1034423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends on which version do you use and how much do you want to ST them as that. In recent books, like the revised era, M20 and the new convention books they aren1t so much like that. They like to picture themselves as such and sure, the Traditions are also buying into the omnipresent enemy thing, because that's easier to rally against. But according the books I read (and I admit I didn't read a lot of 1e-2e books yet) they really aren't that way. They have very limited resources, most importantly in the manpower side of things. They're sretching <i>very </i>thin, because there's a very limited number of people awakening in a given time and they have only a portion of them. Yes, they have fingers in a lot of pies and they have access to a lot of things, like government institutions and law enforcement but they can't survey everything constantly and you don't want to share inner things with the sleeper subordinates, or send said subordinates against supernatural threats. Yes, if you are making noise and bring attention on yourself and becoming a major problem, they could strike with a lot of concentrated force, but normally they can't monitor everything an be everywhere.<br /> <br /> Or look at it that way: if they were really omnipresent and omnipowerfull, they'd have eradicated the traditions and every other supernatural critters a long time ago. But they didn't, because they can't.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I don't agree with you conclusion that they make sense only as an omnipresent thing. Yes they're powerful, but they aren't the only ones. They don't clash with the Camarilla, or the Pentex in all-out war, because in reality, you go to war, if you have a reasonably good chance to win without too much loss knowing if you lose too much, a laughing third party would saunter in and swipe the floor with you. That, and Vampires tend to be minding their own business and stay out of the way. Until they don't and then, you'd need to bring out the bombs and sun-lasers. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Being the most powerful group in any given game doesn't necessiate in my book that they must control everything. Yes, they likely the biggest dog in WoD, but don't think in absolutes, they're other not much smaller dogs. They could be menacing, extremely powerful and dangerous without invalidating every other group, IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Union doesn't need to be <i>Deus Ex Machinae</i> on the WoD. Their propaganda is enough for their role as &quot;The Big Brother&quot; of the world. And I know they have their hands full, at any given moment. I haven't disregard that. But like Goebbels said &quot;a lie told 1.000 times becomes a truth&quot;, the propaganda should suffice to convince the vampires to keep their masqerade, or any other group to follow similar protocol. The Traditions don't fight the Union because they are bold and think they have a chance, they do it <b>because no one else will</b>. The traditions believe that the final victory of the Union would be just slightly better than a victory of the Nafandi. If not for the Ascension War, the Traditions would do the same as the vampires: hide and survive. Which is what they do after the Avatar Storm and the realization that the war was over, and that they <i>lost</i>.<br /> <br /> Should all the denizens of the WoD unite, the Union would vanish. True enough. But that will never happen. So, why would the Camarilla start a war that it cannot win alone against them? To have a glorious death and give freedom back to the Sabbath, Garou and Traditions? No group would do that, so the smartest thing to do is to hide from their anger. And let others weaken them while being crushed.<br /> <br /> The war of the Traditions is the same of the Garou... Its a lost battle, but they must keep fighting, cuz no one else will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T21:22:16-08:00","id":1034449,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">[QUOTE=Karlgust;n1034432] And it gets even worse for other games... For example, the Pentex, probably the greatest enemy of ALL the shapeshifters, is part of the Union. A small part of it, to be honest. The entire Pentex is inside the Division Q, a Methodology of the Syndicate. Ok, lets give it some guessed numbers to try to understand: the Syndicate is one out if 5 conventions. Perhaps, Division Q of the Syndicate answers for about one fifth of the entire Syndicate. And Pentex is half of that Methodology. So, 5 x 5 x 2 = 50. That means that the feared organization of the Wyrm answers for only 1/50 of the amount of the power of the Union.[</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">/QUOTE]</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1034440#post1034440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry, but where that even came from???<br /> <br /> As far as I know, the Pentex is most certainly not the part of the Union. There might be mutual projects and occasional alliances, but in the big picture they're more rivals than friends.</div> </div> </div> </div>Karlgrust is misrepresenting the situation entirely.<br /> <br /> The Special Projects Division of the Syndicate (not Q Division, that's New World Order) has a working relationship with, and has been corrupted by, Pentex. It's Pentex's point of infiltration into the Union, it's not &quot;Pentex is only 1/50th the full power of the Union!&quot;. If and when the true nature of what Special Projects Division has become is exposed to the rest of the Union, they would be hunted down as the Malfean Nephandi &quot;reality deviants&quot; that they are. This more or less happens in the Revised Syndicate Convention book (I believe Mage20th takes a metaplot agnostic view on whether it's happened yet), though SPD goes off the grid rather than be hunted down. When Syndicate agents are sent to Pentex facilities to investigate any traces of their former agents, heads of the investigating agents tend to arrive back at Union fronts in boxes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 01-19-2017, 12:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T21:27:01-08:00","id":1034452,"title":"","content":"By the way, were is the Wyrm in the WoD? The forces of the Wyrm WILL engulf the creation into final destruction, and they vastly outnumber the forces of the Champions of Gaia. If the Garou suffer final defeat, it's the Void for everyone.<br /> <br /> And yet, no Vampire seems to bother. By the way, the forces of Wyrm doesn't care about no Vampire either, except for the occasional rare infernalist or Baali.<br /> <br /> Mages don't like Nefandi, but they are busy trying to hold the keys of Consensus. Maybe they don't think the Wyrm is such a big threat after all... Hunting Deviants or fighting the Union seems more important to them. Its not like the world will end anyway right... So, stoping those nocive notions of &quot;science&quot; or &quot;magik&quot; is the first priority, since its a bigger threat than a feel entropic forces playing games...<br /> <br /> You see, any of those world views are broken","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T21:33:50-08:00","id":1034455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1034452#post1034452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, were is the Wyrm in the WoD? The forces of the Wyrm WILL engulf the creation into final destruction, and they vastly outnumber the forces of the Champions of Gaia. If the Garou suffer final defeat, it's the Void for everyone.<br /> <br /> And yet, no Vampire seems to bother. By the way, the forces of Wyrm doesn't care about no Vampire either, except for the occasional rare infernalist or Baali.<br /> <br /> Mages don't like Nefandi, but they are busy trying to hold the keys of Consensus. Maybe they don't think the Wyrm is such a big threat after all... Hunting Deviants or fighting the Union seems more important to them. Its not like the world will end anyway right... So, stoping those nocive notions of &quot;science&quot; or &quot;magik&quot; is the first priority, since its a bigger threat than a feel entropic forces playing games...<br /> <br /> You see, any of those world views are broken</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Vampires overwhelmingly have no awareness of the spiritual, so I don't know what point you're trying to make there.<br /> <br /> Mages interact with the universe through different paradigms. The spiritual war the Garou are part of is one such paradigm. The threat posed by the Wyrm manifests completely differently with completely different causes in other paradigms. Welcome to Consensual Reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T21:42:47-08:00","id":1034457,"title":"","content":"Ok, obviously the entire Pentex is not under the strong fist of the Union (for obvious reasons). We could roughly say that has one foot in and one out. 50/50. But they work closely with the Union, and a good part of the SPD methodology (thanks for the correction) is on the Pentex pocket. So, it's a conspiracy inside a conspiracy, so it's really hard to say were one begins and another ends. The Syndicate is however, buying many of their technotoys that those boys are making, since its a pragmatic convention and not reserching one, like the Progenitors or Iteration X, and SPD is having amazing progress in very little time (because they use Banes to cheat and produce tainted techno fetiches). So, you could say that perhaps Pentex is, at least officially, INSIDE the Union (of course they have another hidden agenda, which means they are 100% out, but the Union doesn't know that until they do)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T21:58:20-08:00","id":1034458,"title":"","content":"SPD creating Bane-Fetish tools for Technocrats was indeed the case in Second Edition. Like I said, Revised Edition has the whole thing come crashing down.<br /> <br /> I don't think the &quot;50/50&quot; characterization was ever remotely accurate though. Pentex having successfully corrupted one Methodology of the Syndicate into their agents in the Union (agents who would be purged if they were exposed) does not equate to Pentex being half-Union. You could argue &quot;Special Projects Division (who are largely Malfean Nephandi barabi) is basically half Pentex&quot; reasonably, but that's it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 01-19-2017, 01:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T22:07:44-08:00","id":1034461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1034455#post1034455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Vampires overwhelmingly have no awareness of the spiritual, so I don't know what point you're trying to make there.<br /> <br /> Mages interact with the universe through different paradigms. The spiritual war the Garou are part of is one such paradigm. The threat posed by the Wyrm manifests completely differently with completely different causes in other paradigms. Welcome to Consensual Reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does that mean that the vampires and mages are totally oblivious to the very real consequences of those spiritual forces? Do you mean that no Giovanni will ever realize that some strings are being pulled by some unknow organization that interfere with his businesses, and will never find out after some investigation that this organization have very... Weird, to say the least, modus operandi, that may verge on the irrational? (why is that Pentex corp that ruined my aquisition of the water treatment plant using so much resouces to send that water to Japan? In my hands, that water would be making money, but in theirs, they are wasting money without a good explanation...) Vampires are paranoid, are you saying that ALL the forces of Wyrm would be able to be totally bellow the radar of ALL the kindred or mages? A Camarilla coterie, investigating Garou activity, would never find the correlation with Pentex?<br /> <br /> Well, in the Book of the Technocracy, it says that the Union started getting suspicious, and started investigating. Also, they found weird the bigger amount of Garou attacks that Pentex suffered, high above the average.<br /> <br /> Why couldn't others notice that too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T08:47:21-08:00","id":1034630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1034461#post1034461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does that mean that the vampires and mages are totally oblivious to the very real consequences of those spiritual forces? Do you mean that no Giovanni will ever realize that some strings are being pulled by some unknow organization that interfere with his businesses, and will never find out after some investigation that this organization have very... Weird, to say the least, modus operandi, that may verge on the irrational?</div> </div> </div> </div>It means that none of the gamelines are really written with the other gamelines as much of an influence, and that if you want to do an even crossover you need to derivate from the books as written, and change the behavior of the individual groups to take more note of the other.<br /> It's as simple as that, really. You can't take the books as absolute reference, b<i>ecause the books are not written from that perspective</i> aside of some courtesy nods here and there, and the 'here are some short opinion pieces of the faction about the other splats' sections. You need to make up status quo adjustments overall <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Else, as I said, things clash and don't really mesh well.<br /> <br /> So yes, if you mix up all the lores evenly, then Vampire business tycoons would definitely notice the Syndicate's influence and investigate it. Mages might much more notice Banes, Fomori and their ilk in the spiritscape, and taint in products.<br /> <br /> Et cetera, et cetera.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T10:41:05-08:00","id":1034707,"title":"","content":"Mages who notice the plans of the Wyrm tend to not survive the experience. The agents of the Wyrm are willing to let their Nephandi allies handle Mages until the Mages in question becomes a threat to their plans. Then the Banes come swarming across the Gauntlet and the Fomori come up through the sewer pipes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T12:31:38-08:00","id":1034783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1034707#post1034707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages who notice the plans of the Wyrm tend to not survive the experience. The agents of the Wyrm are willing to let their Nephandi allies handle Mages until the Mages in question becomes a threat to their plans. Then the Banes come swarming across the Gauntlet and the Fomori come up through the sewer pipes.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's, again, a shallow view. One single Mage can be easy pray. But so, would a single Garou. But what you're saying implies that the Traditions or the Technocracy, as WHOLE groups, are completely oblivious to the machinachions of the Wyrm agents. Because, if those groups have knowledge about that, why haven't the Wyrm destroyed the Traditions or the Union yet? (short answer: because that is as hard, or more, as destroying the Garou).<br /> <br /> Two mistakes here: you are thinking on terms of game mechanics, and you do consider mages feeble beings (it's not the first time you do). Secondly, you're thinking on an individual level, which is also why you think mages are weak (because they can't survive rockets explosions and can't rip steel with their bare hands, like Garou). As a group, mages may well be the most powerful beings of WoD, even if individually they aint.<br /> <br /> I highly doubt that any werewolf, from many packs, protecting a powerful Caern, could survive a direct assault from a single Qui La Machine from the Void Engeneers (a powerful Starship vessel from the VE to explore other dimensions).<br /> <br /> Besides, that's not the point. You're rationalizing the question, &quot;trying to fit reality to your paradigm&quot;, like many others. But the reality is exactly what Ambrosia said: those games simply don't fit toghether.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T13:22:28-08:00","id":1034826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1034404#post1034404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My advice?<br /> <br /> Or, to put it differently, what a rokea would remeber?</div> </div> </div> </div>Crazy Lovecraftian shit - fighting the Chulorviah elders toe to toe, staring down the vast, Cthulhu-esque thing that was Nightmare before it shrank down and became the progenitor of the Merdhuacha, pre-human wars waged against the Mokole and Ananasi, prehistoric wars around human time, war just about any other time in their existence because this is Werewolf and it's a game about war and its cost...<br /> <br /> Finding elders with colorful eons-long personal histories, though, is going to be difficult, because they tend to swim off into rarer parts of the Umbra after a while.<br /> <br /> Now, the time before, say, a Greenland shark's long swim? That's going to seem like a whole lot of nothing, because those sharks mature on the same time scale as an old school D&amp;D elf (i.e. roughly ten times longer than a human). But after that, the Rokea life can be very eventful, since they all still have Rage and opinions on important matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T13:43:56-08:00","id":1034842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1034826#post1034826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Crazy Lovecraftian shit - fighting the Chulorviah elders toe to toe, staring down the vast, Cthulhu-esque thing that was Nightmare before it shrank down and became the progenitor of the Merdhuacha, pre-human wars waged against the Mokole and Ananasi, prehistoric wars around human time, war just about any other time in their existence because this is Werewolf and it's a game about war and its cost...<br /> <br /> Finding elders with colorful eons-long personal histories, though, is going to be difficult, because they tend to swim off into rarer parts of the Umbra after a while.<br /> <br /> Now, the time before, say, a Greenland shark's long swim? That's going to seem like a whole lot of nothing, because those sharks mature on the same time scale as an old school D&amp;D elf (i.e. roughly ten times longer than a human). But after that, the Rokea life can be very eventful, since they all still have Rage and opinions on important matters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do they keep track of time?<br /> <br /> &quot;Now, lets see... Last time I fough an Ichtyossaurus were 10.000 years ago, or 100.000 million years? I can't remember exactly now...&quot;<br /> <br /> Because if they don't, those memories would only be a huge amount of unlinear moments... And their heads would be a mess","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T13:50:11-08:00","id":1034849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1034842#post1034842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do they keep track of time?</div> </div> </div> </div>They have the stars in the sky to look at, so probably, yes. Most sharks tend to swim closer to the surface to partially navigate by day and starlight, so the Rokea would have a fair bit to build on. The Mokole were also avid watchers of the night sky, even if you don't go for the Quintaglio &quot;adaptation&quot; in the breed book, and the Ananasi like patterns, so the three together could have been starwatching together for ages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T14:41:57-08:00","id":1034872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1034461#post1034461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does that mean that the vampires and mages are totally oblivious to the very real consequences of those spiritual forces? Do you mean that no Giovanni will ever realize that some strings are being pulled by some unknow organization that interfere with his businesses, and will never find out after some investigation that this organization have very... Weird, to say the least, modus operandi, that may verge on the irrational? (why is that Pentex corp that ruined my aquisition of the water treatment plant using so much resouces to send that water to Japan? In my hands, that water would be making money, but in theirs, they are wasting money without a good explanation...) Vampires are paranoid, are you saying that ALL the forces of Wyrm would be able to be totally bellow the radar of ALL the kindred or mages? A Camarilla coterie, investigating Garou activity, would never find the correlation with Pentex?<br /> <br /> Well, in the Book of the Technocracy, it says that the Union started getting suspicious, and started investigating. Also, they found weird the bigger amount of Garou attacks that Pentex suffered, high above the average.<br /> <br /> Why couldn't others notice that too?</div> </div> </div> </div>Look, what's really your goal? You want to convince people that crossover is impossible? It's not, a lot of people did and are doing it. Yes, you'd make some changes here and there, to having all those big conspiracies and organizations working at he same time, because the games weren't written with that goal. But it's doable and necessary only, if you want to go all the way to the upper echelons of WoD with your chronicle. With a smaller scope, it's even easier.<br /> <br /> Besides, i think a lot of people, who're talking about how those things don't work simultaneously make the mistake assuming that individuals in the WoD are organized and communicating. Basically it's mistaking reader/player knowledge with character knowledge. For example the above &quot;problem&quot; with the Wyrm. From an average Mage standpoint that's some weird spirit and werewolf religion crap. Oh yes, there are tainted spirits out there and possessed people (they'd probably rationalize it as infernalists and nephandi) and whatnot and occasionally they're causing trouble and need to be deal with. But they don't know about any global Wyrm conspiracy. Even all of the Garou don't know about the entirety of Pentex. An individual mage, or cabal might be on good terms with the Garou, even listening to what they're saying and believing in it and helping them in the fight, but it's a minority. However, they're most likely don't share their knowledge and experience with all the mages, because they just don't have a way to do it, reliably and besides most other mages wouldn't believe in them and won't want to deal with this hippy thing when the Technocracy is knocking on the door. And yes that stands even if Horizon is still standing. Even the masters have limited knowledge and a lot of personal biases and flaws. Think about it: there are a lot of people out there now who sincerely think there's no such a thing as global warming. Just think about it. It's not a conspiracy, it's a well-known thing with a ton of evidence, acknowledged worldwide. Still some people just don't believe in it and there are politicians speaking against it.<br /> <br /> You say this and that wouldn't work, because groups would notice and do something. I say, no that doesn't work like that, people in general are waaaaay more stupid than that. They don't get the big picture, or don't know enough, or can't convince enough other people, or just choose to deal with other problems which seemed to be more imminent from their viewpoint. People are stupid, short-sighted, narrow-minded, factious things. Think about how much must happened during the second WW before the Allied forces amassed something that resembled cooperation.<br /> <br /> A good in-game example IMO is the second Massasa War. Even in the much tighter group of the OoH, the left hand didn't know what the right's doing and they didn't know shit about the vampires they're going against.<br /> <br /> Also, another thing that tends to be forgotten is that there aren't that much supernatural individuals out there. It seems so that they and their wars are everywhere (because these are games about them and those, duh...), but in reality, according to the books, even a full-blown Sabbat siege could be covered as a turf war. And there are much more vampires than mages, or werewolves. That puts it in perspective, I think. The big conspiracies, they're hiding themselves really well, even from their subordinates and especially from each other. A Giovanni might notice that there is <i>some </i>organization behind the groups she's dealing with on the stock market, but she would need to do a lot, <i>lot </i>of research and in very obscure ways to find out any real evidence. It's not like the leaders of the Pentex, NWO, Syndicate, Camarilla and Giovanni holding an Evil V5 Conference each year.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 01-19-2017, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T14:49:03-08:00","id":1034876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1034826#post1034826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Crazy Lovecraftian shit - fighting the Chulorviah elders toe to toe, staring down the vast, Cthulhu-esque thing that was Nightmare before it shrank down and became the progenitor of the Merdhuacha, pre-human wars waged against the Mokole and Ananasi, prehistoric wars around human time, war just about any other time in their existence because this is Werewolf and it's a game about war and its cost...<br /> <br /> Finding elders with colorful eons-long personal histories, though, is going to be difficult, because they tend to swim off into rarer parts of the Umbra after a while.<br /> <br /> Now, the time before, say, a Greenland shark's long swim? That's going to seem like a whole lot of nothing, because those sharks mature on the same time scale as an old school D&amp;D elf (i.e. roughly ten times longer than a human). But after that, the Rokea life can be very eventful, since they all still have Rage and opinions on important matters.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's interesting, I need to read more about them...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They have the stars in the sky to look at, so probably, yes. Most sharks tend to swim closer to the surface to partially navigate by day and starlight, so the Rokea would have a fair bit to build on. The Mokole were also avid watchers of the night sky, even if you don't go for the Quintaglio &quot;adaptation&quot; in the breed book, and the Ananasi like patterns, so the three together could have been starwatching together for ages. </div> </div> </div>I1m still keeping my opinion that the problem with non-written history and oral tradition and personal memories is that it's even more unreliable than the written sources by an order of magnitude. Those stories about those hings you mentioned are much more like &quot;Once upon a time, long ago, there was this great evil and the brave heroen went against it, etc, etc.&quot; Those are educational stories and myths, not exact historical records. You could go and find an elder in the far reaches of the umbra, just like you could find a methuselah to start asking questions, but even for them, memories got hazy. How much do you remember from 5 years ago? 10 years? Bits and pieces, the most important things. And even then, those ages-old creatures saw just a part of the things, not the entirety of any event much less history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T15:55:47-08:00","id":1034909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1034876#post1034876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I1m still keeping my opinion that the problem with non-written history and oral tradition and personal memories is that it's even more unreliable than the written sources by an order of magnitude. Those stories about those hings you mentioned are much more like &quot;Once upon a time, long ago, there was this great evil and the brave heroen went against it, etc, etc.&quot; Those are educational stories and myths, not exact historical records. You could go and find an elder in the far reaches of the umbra, just like you could find a methuselah to start asking questions, but even for them, memories got hazy. How much do you remember from 5 years ago? 10 years? Bits and pieces, the most important things. And even then, those ages-old creatures saw just a part of the things, not the entirety of any event much less history.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see two problems with this line of thought. The first is that inter-generational storytelling changes accounts into myth... but this is not as much of an issue for creatures like Mokole or Rokea. The Rokea in particular can theoretically live forever, therefore their oral history isn't quite as likely to be obscured by the ages. Information isn't passed down through the eons via dozens or hundreds of storytellers, it can be received from 1st, 2nd, or 3rd hand sources.<br /> <br /> Second, our current modern western perception of needing rigorous scientific accuracy regarding history is quite new. The chroniclers and historians of old were never so precise; usually they wrote with specific narrative motive, and 100% verifiable truth wasn't it. Myth is not necessarily bad or even <i>wrong</i>. When an elder says 'this story is true,' they mean it, but not necessarily in a way that would satisfy Wikipedia. The moral or message of the story is what is important, not the precise gritty details that we currently value so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 01-19-2017, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T16:06:17-08:00","id":1034916,"title":"","content":"However, even 1st hand recalls of, for example, felonies are unreliable. Eyewitnesses just don't perceive reliably. And there's the problem of what I wrote above, that individuals saw only their immediate vicinity.<br /> <br /> That those stories aren't meant to be historical records in the modern sense, but morals is true and fine, but it doesn't contradict my initial point that the denizens of WoD don't know their exact history, but largely know myths and contradiction among them is not something that exclude them working in the same setting, IMO.<br /> <br /> The far past of WoD is highly malleable and basically a very big &quot;We don't know&quot; in my book. And it's fine, I don't need an unified creation story for every game. Real people have different faiths, it actually adds to the setting that different supernaturals have theirs too, at least for me.<br /> <br /> Edit: oh, I might add, that yes, sometimes the important parts gone missing among the gritty details we're focusing on nowadays, but on the other hand, a story is much more prone to bending and shaping to comfort the storyteller's goals. And that's how you get misconceptions and false history and likely that's how it happened in WoD too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 01-19-2017, 07:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T20:20:48-08:00","id":1035029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1034916#post1034916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, even 1st hand recalls of, for example, felonies are unreliable. Eyewitnesses just don't perceive reliably. And there's the problem of what I wrote above, that individuals saw only their immediate vicinity.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a first rank Gift called Perfect Recall. It does pretty much exactly what the name would suggest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That those stories aren't meant to be historical records in the modern sense, but morals is true and fine, but it doesn't contradict my initial point that the denizens of WoD don't know their exact history, but largely know myths and contradiction among them is not something that exclude them working in the same setting, IMO.<br /> <br /> The far past of WoD is highly malleable and basically a very big &quot;We don't know&quot; in my book. And it's fine, I don't need an unified creation story for every game. Real people have different faiths, it actually adds to the setting that different supernaturals have theirs too, at least for me.<br /> <br /> Edit: oh, I might add, that yes, sometimes the important parts gone missing among the gritty details we're focusing on nowadays, but on the other hand, a story is much more prone to bending and shaping to comfort the storyteller's goals. And that's how you get misconceptions and false history and likely that's how it happened in WoD too. </div> </div> </div>If you're writing a game where someone needs to know something very, very old, then the Mokole, Rokea, and Ananasi would probably know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T20:44:45-08:00","id":1035038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1035029#post1035029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're writing a game where someone needs to know something very, very old, then the Mokole, Rokea, and Ananasi would probably know.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's almost like it could be one of their divinely determined purpose for existence <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Which in a crossover counts for next to nothing unfortunately (since someone's game line is getting screwed), which is the point of this thread.<br /> But within the realm of WtA I 100% agree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T23:04:07-08:00","id":1035100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1035029#post1035029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a first rank Gift called Perfect Recall. It does pretty much exactly what the name would suggest.<br /> <br /> If you're writing a game where someone needs to know something very, very old, then the Mokole, Rokea, and Ananasi would probably know.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So? That's still one person's memory. Even them weren't here to witness every, or just a tangible portion of history. We're speaking about individuals whose numbers might be aren't over several hundreds. What they could have witnessed is very limited in scope.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1035038#post1035038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's almost like it could be one of their divinely determined purpose for existence <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Which in a crossover counts for next to nothing unfortunately (since someone's game line is getting screwed), which is the point of this thread.<br /> But within the realm of WtA I 100% agree.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing. I'm on the firm opinion that yes, a total crossover game have a different setting than a game focusing on just one splat, but it's not &quot;getting screwed&quot; for me. Things would need readjusting, relationships mapping, etc. But that's it.<br /> <br /> It's a silly analogue, but the Justice League isn't about Batman and Batman's problems, or Flash, or any of them. It's about the team and the problems they're facing together. A crossover game is not bad, because it doesn't prefers one game's mythology/enemy/whatnot over the others. That's not the purpose of it. That's just not &quot;getting screwed&quot; in my book, it's just acknowledging that this chronicle's world and setting is not about your favorite splat and your splat's problem, while could be very important, depending on the story, are not necessarily the most important things going on in any given time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T09:57:08-08:00","id":1035286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1034424#post1034424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But why did the little Tremere crossed the tzimisce road?<br /> <br /> Well, first of all, the Tremere were MAGES. Not sorcerous, not stage tricksters. They were Awakened.<br /> <br /> But not just anyone: they were of the founding houses of the Hermetic Order. Very specific.<br /> <br /> So, why did Tremere decided to become a Vampire?<br /> <br /> Well... He felt &quot;a disturbance in the force&quot;. He predicted that his imortal alchemical drugs would stop working, after centuries of using them just fine, thanks.<br /> <br /> But... WHY? Why would they stop working out of the blue?<br /> <br /> Because of the SCOURGE (PARADOX). Basically, Tremere divinated a world were mages wouldn't be able to get away with massing with the reality any more.<br /> <br /> But... What's the orign of the Scourge?<br /> <br /> It comes from the Consensus.<br /> <br /> Thing is, the Consensus were the thing that the Order of Reason were creating. No Order of Reason, no Consensus, no Scourge, no Tremere vampires. Simple.<br /> <br /> And we can't just remove the Tremere from VtM, that would mess things up... No Tremere, the Salubri are back, no anarchist revolt, no Camarilla, no Sabbat (Im now pretty sure that all of that must be the work of an Entropy m\u00e1ster... Just picture the image of an Entropy 5 effect on Tremere that made him &quot;imagine a world with no magik. Funny idea).<br /> <br /> So, the Order of Reason is a NECESSITY for VtM... Even if all that chain of events is invisible to ALL kindred</div> </div> </div> </div>So the Order of Reason, founded in 1325 went out to create the Consensus which caused Tremere to wig out when his immortality potions were beginning to fail....<br /> <br /> But Tremere wigged out and started studying vampirism, 300 years before the Order of Reason was founded. <br /> <br /> There is a causality issues here.<br /> <br /> Also, no Consensus during the Dark Ages. No Paradox. No Scourge. Sometimes your spells just went fizzle but that didn't cause any more issues than a botch does for any other sort of supernatural. If you want to go all Ars Magica, there was the Dominion as a sort of &quot;Consensus-precursor&quot; that interfered with the Hermetic magic (and others) while enabling the Messianic Voices and usually associated with settlements (the one's with churches and cathedrals), but that's more Reality Zones and impeded magic does not Paradox make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T10:36:10-08:00","id":1035305,"title":"","content":"I though that there was something like Paradox in Dark Ages: Mage. I think the problem that Tremere had was that he had already lived too long and was too set in his ways to accept the changing tides of magic. Instead of accepting that 500+ years was probably the most that he could get from True Magick, he tried to cheat and ended up with the false immortality of the Kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T13:33:33-08:00","id":1035419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1035100#post1035100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So? That's still one person's memory. Even them weren't here to witness every, or just a tangible portion of history. We're speaking about individuals whose numbers might be aren't over several hundreds. What they could have witnessed is very limited in scope.</div> </div> </div> </div>Recall that we're dealing with beings that have frequent mystic visions warning them of looming calamities, the capacity to cheat the separation of space to cut travel time significantly, and a social-spiritual mandate to go and involve themselves in dangerous shit. They might not have every base covered, but they'll have had a rather large body of interesting experiences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T13:56:56-08:00","id":1035434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1035419#post1035419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Recall that we're dealing with beings that have frequent mystic visions warning them of looming calamities, the capacity to cheat the separation of space to cut travel time significantly, and a social-spiritual mandate to go and involve themselves in dangerous shit. They might not have every base covered, but they'll have had a rather large body of interesting experiences.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are they perfectly all-knowing to the point of being mistakes-proof?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T13:58:58-08:00","id":1035435,"title":"","content":"If they know so much, why didn't they crushed those troublesome &quot;naked apes&quot; when they first descented from the trees before all the shit hit the fan?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T14:00:55-08:00","id":1035436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1035435#post1035435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they know so much, why didn't they crushed those troublesome &quot;naked apes&quot; when they first descented from the trees before all the shit hit the fan?</div> </div> </div> </div>Who do you think culled their ancestors and got them out from the trees in the first place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T14:03:03-08:00","id":1035437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1035286#post1035286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So the Order of Reason, founded in 1325 went out to create the Consensus which caused Tremere to wig out when his immortality potions were beginning to fail....<br /> <br /> But Tremere wigged out and started studying vampirism, 300 years before the Order of Reason was founded. <br /> <br /> There is a causality issues here.<br /> <br /> Also, no Consensus during the Dark Ages. No Paradox. No Scourge. Sometimes your spells just went fizzle but that didn't cause any more issues than a botch does for any other sort of supernatural. If you want to go all Ars Magica, there was the Dominion as a sort of &amp;quot;Consensus-precursor&amp;quot; that interfered with the Hermetic magic (and others) while enabling the Messianic Voices and usually associated with settlements (the one's with churches and cathedrals), but that's more Reality Zones and impeded magic does not Paradox make.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hum... Ok, maybe it were a misinterpretation I had... I always thought that happened because he had a vision that his drugs would cease to work allthogether, and that they were starting to give him bad trips as an &quot;prior effect&quot; of sorts from what would be Consensus later","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T14:15:55-08:00","id":1035445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1034872#post1034872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Look, what's really your goal? You want to convince people that crossover is impossible? It's not, a lot of people did and are doing it. Yes, you'd make some changes here and there, to having all those big conspiracies and organizations working at he same time, because the games weren't written with that goal. But it's doable and necessary only, if you want to go all the way to the upper echelons of WoD with your chronicle. With a smaller scope, it's even easier.<br /> <br /> Besides, i think a lot of people, who're talking about how those things don't work simultaneously make the mistake assuming that individuals in the WoD are organized and communicating. Basically it's mistaking reader/player knowledge with character knowledge. For example the above &amp;quot;problem&amp;quot; with the Wyrm. From an average Mage standpoint that's some weird spirit and werewolf religion crap. Oh yes, there are tainted spirits out there and possessed people (they'd probably rationalize it as infernalists and nephandi) and whatnot and occasionally they're causing trouble and need to be deal with. But they don't know about any global Wyrm conspiracy. Even all of the Garou don't know about the entirety of Pentex. An individual mage, or cabal might be on good terms with the Garou, even listening to what they're saying and believing in it and helping them in the fight, but it's a minority. However, they're most likely don't share their knowledge and experience with all the mages, because they just don't have a way to do it, reliably and besides most other mages wouldn't believe in them and won't want to deal with this hippy thing when the Technocracy is knocking on the door. And yes that stands even if Horizon is still standing. Even the masters have limited knowledge and a lot of personal biases and flaws. Think about it: there are a lot of people out there now who sincerely think there's no such a thing as global warming. Just think about it. It's not a conspiracy, it's a well-known thing with a ton of evidence, acknowledged worldwide. Still some people just don't believe in it and there are politicians speaking against it.<br /> <br /> You say this and that wouldn't work, because groups would notice and do something. I say, no that doesn't work like that, people in general are waaaaay more stupid than that. They don't get the big picture, or don't know enough, or can't convince enough other people, or just choose to deal with other problems which seemed to be more imminent from their viewpoint. People are stupid, short-sighted, narrow-minded, factious things. Think about how much must happened during the second WW before the Allied forces amassed something that resembled cooperation.<br /> <br /> A good in-game example IMO is the second Massasa War. Even in the much tighter group of the OoH, the left hand didn't know what the right's doing and they didn't know shit about the vampires they're going against.<br /> <br /> Also, another thing that tends to be forgotten is that there aren't that much supernatural individuals out there. It seems so that they and their wars are everywhere (because these are games about them and those, duh...), but in reality, according to the books, even a full-blown Sabbat siege could be covered as a turf war. And there are much more vampires than mages, or werewolves. That puts it in perspective, I think. The big conspiracies, they're hiding themselves really well, even from their subordinates and especially from each other. A Giovanni might notice that there is <i>some </i>organization behind the groups she's dealing with on the stock market, but she would need to do a lot, <i>lot </i>of research and in very obscure ways to find out any real evidence. It's not like the leaders of the Pentex, NWO, Syndicate, Camarilla and Giovanni holding an Evil V5 Conference each year.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I have a communication problem... I don't why, but so many people on so many topics get mad at me, but I'm sincerely not doing on purpose...<br /> <br /> Well... I'm not trying to say &quot;don't do it&quot;. I'm trying to make some good ideas on how to do it<br /> <br /> Another thing that crossed my mind.... Why can't exist this super-secret-conspiracy that has many different types of supernaturals? I mean... Did you ever heard that joke about a Mage, a Vampire, a Garou and a Changelling entering a bar... And creating their own organization?<br /> <br /> Well, the shapeshifters of the East are not organized by their supernatural &quot;race&quot;, instead making &quot; super heores clubs&quot;, were all breeds are toghether (except the Ananasi), and their divisions are cultural/social rather than racial... So, why can't we have the &quot;league of extraordinary monsters&quot;?<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T14:18:00-08:00","id":1035447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1035419#post1035419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Recall that we're dealing with beings that have frequent mystic visions warning them of looming calamities, the capacity to cheat the separation of space to cut travel time significantly, and a social-spiritual mandate to go and involve themselves in dangerous shit. They might not have every base covered, but they'll have had a rather large body of interesting experiences.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are still very few and still can't be everywhere. They can't be in every battle, much less in every back-room negotiating and intrigue. Even if a character was present during an event, what individuals see is, again, very limited and extremely biased. <br /> <br /> Look, vampire elders, methuselahs, archmages and shapeshifters, or any other critter with a very long or infinite lifespan are just not infallible, omniscient repositories of history. They know a lot more about specific things, persons and events, than what is in the books, yes, but the biggest parts of their knowledge are personal impressions, stories and anecdotes. One of them may have war stories about Richard the Lionheart, another may have known Shakespeare personally and read the first draft of Midsummer Night's dream. Another one might been present at the fall of Constantinople. All of that is good, it adds to the game, but it's very different than assuming they know every part of history infallibly and objectively. Besides, those individual immortals and old things are scattered, hard to reach and very low in numbers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T14:36:31-08:00","id":1035456,"title":"","content":"Another thing that just crossed my mind... Since those shifters were around since the Dinos... Does that mean that Evolution is a thing in the cWoD?<br /> <br /> If so, does that mean that the Mokole, Ananasi and Rokea themselves only came to be after reptiles, spiders and sharks evolved?<br /> <br /> That would make the Mokole a lot younger than the others...<br /> <br /> And...<br /> <br /> What other breeds could have gone extinct BEFORE humanity came? Trilobites-shifters? <br /> <br /> And...<br /> <br /> Were the mokole, rokea and ananasi only &quot;animals&quot; with no human part at those times?<br /> <br /> And...<br /> <br /> How did the first animals became part human? Could it be that shifters are akin to fomori, except that its a gaian spirit that fuses with a human at birth and not banes at any point in life? Or would it be more like the changelling way? (Which would bring weight to the claim of the Fae of them being &quot;lost cousins&quot;)<br /> <br /> That also brings me another question I have... Since the spirits of Wyrm can create Fomori... Is it possible to do the same with other kinds of spirits? Is it possible to do a Weaver-fomorian-way or Wyld-fomorian-way, or to do that with High Umbrals or even wraiths (or not sentient plasmics from the Underworld)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T14:39:02-08:00","id":1035458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1035436#post1035436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who do you think culled their ancestors and got them out from the trees in the first place?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why didn't they forsee that Gaia &quot;got that one wrong&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T14:44:31-08:00","id":1035461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1035445#post1035445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I have a communication problem... I don't why, but so many people on so many topics get mad at me, but I'm sincerely not doing on purpose...<br /> <br /> Well... I'm not trying to say &quot;don't do it&quot;. I'm trying to make some good ideas on how to do it</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not mad at all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I was just uncertain about what is your goal with this topic? At first, you asked for advice about crossovers, then went to great lengths about how crossover is bonkers and that was a bit confusing to me.<br /> <br /> Regardless, to maintain a productive conversation:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another thing that crossed my mind.... Why can't exist this super-secret-conspiracy that has many different types of supernaturals? I mean... Did you ever heard that joke about a Mage, a Vampire, a Garou and a Changelling entering a bar... And creating their own organization?<br /> <br /> Well, the shapeshifters of the East are not organized by their supernatural &quot;race&quot;, instead making &quot; super heores clubs&quot;, were all breeds are toghether (except the Ananasi), and their divisions are cultural/social rather than racial... So, why can't we have the &quot;league of extraordinary monsters&quot;?<br /> <br /> What do you guys think? </div> </div> </div>That's a great question and I asked myself that several times. The logical answer is it can't exist, because, while I on the firm opinion that the WoD is intentionally a crossover setting (the corebooks and nearly every supplement mention other critters), the games itself weren't intended as crossover. But basically we all know that, every game has it's own protagonists and focus. Moreover, different writers had different opinions about crossovers. Thus, something like a supernatural coalition, or the aforementioned Evil G5 never happened, the closes things are indeed Pentex, the Beast Courts and maybe the Tal'MaheRA to some extent.<br /> <br /> Now, I <i>do </i>think that something like a supnat coalition could exist, but not on the large scale. You would have a sincerely apocalypse-like event on the big scale to get the big groups working together in concert. Otherwise, there's too much lack of knowledge, misunderstanding, differing interests and goals, limited resources and so on.<br /> <br /> However, on the smaller scale, you absolutely could have something in my opinion, either locally, or on a bigger, organizational level. The Traditions as a whole are likely won't sign a pact with the Garou Nation, but there might be a Dreamspeaker group which maintains an exceptionally good relationship with the Uktena, even maybe with a lot of kinfolk mages and sorcerers. They could even originates from the same tribe and from one region. They could help each other out regularly. I think that's fine, things like that are great foundations for chronicles and character concepts.<br /> <br /> Or, in a contested city between the Camarilla and the Sabbat the local Bone Gnawers and Glasswalkers might have forged a very strenous, but functional (for now..) treaty and pact with the local Camarilla establishment, because at least those leeches are reasonable and tend to stay low and the evil you know is always better.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, while I think a super-secret allied supnat organization is very unlikely, unless you're willing to rewrite large parts of the setting (and I'm not against that, honestly, I'd like to play in a more &quot;conventional urban fantasy&quot; setting too, where the different groups and critters are constituting a more unified underground culture with smaller subcultures, instead of the extremely xenophobic groups of WoD - maybe we'll get a step in that direction with the upcoming One WoD). However, there might be personal avquaintances and friendships and frenemies in the upper echelons of the groups, who could make up a quasi-informal super-conspiracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T15:06:25-08:00","id":1035478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1035458#post1035458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why didn't they forsee that Gaia &quot;got that one wrong&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't Gaia, except in the broadest possible sense of cosmic beings bringing various facets of existence about. It was the Mokole trying to make something like their lost Drachid kin in the apes that they took great care to cull, generation after generation, sleeping between lifetimes or trusting their descendants to do the work for them.<br /> <br /> (I did say that Werewolf's pre-human history got very Lovecraftian, after all.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T16:21:13-08:00","id":1035505,"title":"","content":"Once I was STing a Chronicle that set the players as co-founders of the Order of Reason (but they were members of an upper conspiracy that called themselves &quot;the REAL Ksirafai&quot;, controlled by a powerful entity, but in truth, it were a higly clever Malfean Onceborn Dread Lord, they of course never saw the creature, only his cultists, all full time nephandi, and those nefandi cultists would give 'em all the directives. So, in my game, the PC became pawns for a Death God, thus basically making the Technocracy it's tool, since the PC were the top first of the Union, the &quot;Control of the Control&quot;. They never went nephandi nor they never took all the strings of the Union, but still it gave the alien monstruosity a huge influence amongst the world, IT only needed to play safe and be cunning. Anyway, I digress).<br /> <br /> Anyway, in this Chronicle, the Union made an agreement with the Camarilla... A sort of an &quot;gentlemen's pact&quot;. They would stay away from each others business, and once upon a time, could whisper a thing or two at the wind... That, however, were the biggest secret of both sides, and only Control and the Inner Circle had any knowledge about that... The Inner Circle would use that to get hid of an unwanted Prince once upon a time without getting their hands dirty, and the Union would get valuable Intel on many Deviants... It was a VERY uneasy &quot;cooperation&quot;, and the temptation of double crossing and paranoia had to be adressed regularly, but in the end, that proved almost crucial for both sides to be able to focus their energies on other targets. The PC tryed to cut similar deals with others, but wasn't as succesful","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T16:24:44-08:00","id":1035506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1035478#post1035478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It wasn't Gaia, except in the broadest possible sense of cosmic beings bringing various facets of existence about. It was the Mokole trying to make something like their lost Drachid kin in the apes that they took great care to cull, generation after generation, sleeping between lifetimes or trusting their descendants to do the work for them.<br /> <br /> (I did say that Werewolf's pre-human history got very Lovecraftian, after all.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It is rather hilarious that, at least according to WtA, humans were not perfectly made in the image of God, but imperfectly made in the image of extinct dinosaur men.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T09:56:25-08:00","id":1036136,"title":"","content":"I had a strong tendinitis crisis and couldn't post for a few days. Now I am using a speech to text converter, so I will try to answer some posts. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1034227#post1034227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But how would you grade what parts score for right or wrong unless you had a definite aim for what the resulting crossover-o-rama was going to look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need to agree with any line to have a definite aim for the resulting crossover O Rama. Just build your own thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1034365#post1034365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paradoxically, the gameline in most agreement with the scientific concensus is WTA, as some of the Rokea are old enough to remember the dinosaurs (Rokea are immortal and are really good at surviving). After the fall of the Second City, WtA and VtM concur on dates, which suggests that the Antediluvian Kindred may be refugees from the Astral Umbra.<br /> <br /> If that was the case, Caine would be an Incarna created by the Godhead of the Astral Umbra to represent the concept of Betrayal who figured out how to become something else. He created the 2nd and 3rd Generation within his Astral Realm and kicked out the 3rd Generation when they killed the 2nd Generation. The 3rd Generation possessed mortals and transformed them into the first Kindred (which would make Kindred strangely like the Changeling interpretation of their origin). It would also explain some of the Mage confusion with the nature of the Kindred and why Risen can learn some Kindred Disciplines (Risen being similar to the first Kindred).</div> </div> </div> </div>This one is actually a pretty good idea. I will borrow it. I was in need for something to explain the Kindred being like in vtm, rules wise, on my wTA game. These will fit perfectly. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1034404#post1034404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My advice?<br /> <br /> First: give up the notion of one convenient, unified timeline and the &quot;this is how things happened and that was how the world was created&quot; approach of other rpgs and worlds.<br /> <br /> Second: base things on the fact that people are fallible. Memories are fallible, even the memories of beings like methuselahs and mokol\u00e9. Oral tradition is <i>extremely </i>fallible. That that garou say something doesn't make it true, it's a <i>myth</i>. Just because something is in a written source, like the Book of Nod doesn't make it true either, just like in real life. Oh, people are whining about Demon, but honestly, demons don't have the truth either. <i>Their </i>God could have been a lot of things. Just because a game was based on Judeo-Christian mythology and another on animistic faith systems doesn't necessiate that either of them have to be exclusively true.<br /> <br /> IMO, when you embrace that no one has the ultimate truth, just their specific mythos, suddenly the &quot;incompatible&quot; worldviews and creation stories start to matter much less. Accidentally that's how the real world works. Different people and religions have very different ideas about how creation works and how it came to exist.<br /> <br /> In my book the different critters having different stories don't deride the game, on the contrary, it adds to it.<br /> <br /> Going back to history: to me, everything earlier than the high middle ages is <i>extremely </i>fragmented, just like in real life. Rome, we know a bit more about, but that's it. Individuals from those ages, like methuselahs usually aren't willing to give up their knowledge, but if they are, they are still <i>individuals </i>and they can't remember something that didn't happen with them personally in an age before fast travel and communication. Even the antediluvians and <i>even Caine</i> are just persons.<br /> <br /> Or, to put it differently, what a rokea would remeber? Swimming, swimming, swimming. A Plesiosaurus here, an early whale there. Bajilion of fish. More swimming. A tasty seal from not so long ago. History tends to not happening in the deep oceans.<br /> <br /> Everything before the great ancient civilizations is basically a myth and no one knows.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ultimately that's what I most agree with. Crossover in the world of Darkness have three kinds of problems: Inconsistent rules, inconsistent perception of current cosmology, and inconsistent assertions on lore. But the last one isn't so much of a problem, only when such assertions can't be ignored. And the fact is that most players put a lot more of weight on those assertions than they actually have.<br /> <br /> <br /> I am still getting used to it, so I won't go any further in the thread. I'm tired and my hand still hurts, so sorry for not participation too much on the conversation, but I have to lay down a little.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T11:32:14-08:00","id":1036192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1036136#post1036136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I had a strong tendinitis crisis and couldn't post for a few days. Now I am using a speech to text converter, so I will try to answer some posts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Feel better soon.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1036136#post1036136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately that's what I most agree with. Crossover in the world of Darkness have three kinds of problems: Inconsistent rules, inconsistent perception of current cosmology, and inconsistent assertions on lore. But the last one isn't so much of a problem, only when such assertions can't be ignored. And the fact is that most players put a lot more of weight on those assertions than they actually have.</div> </div> </div> </div>The last one is mainly a problem in world building, from the ST perspective. I find it rarely comes up in game (referring to IC in crossover games). But the Players can and do sometimes still have issues with how the world is set up, even if their characters aren't going to know anything about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T12:03:05-08:00","id":1036209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1036136#post1036136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This one is actually a pretty good idea. I will borrow it. I was in need for something to explain the Kindred being like in vtm, rules wise, on my wTA game. These will fit perfectly.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, it is still a rough idea, but I think it satisfactorily explains the strange connection of the Kindred to the Astral Umbra. The 3rd generation would have probably visited the Earth many times (starting in 8000 BC) before they were permanently exiled (probably around 4000 BC). During that 4000 year period, they would have sired the first members of the 4th generation, most of whom were probably killed off by Fae, Garou, Mages, or stranger things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T13:58:52-08:00","id":1036263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1036136#post1036136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a strong tendinitis crisis and couldn't post for a few days. Now I am using a speech to text converter, so I will try to answer some posts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wish you fast recovery! I had tendonitis some years ago. It got well with several weeks of resting and then light, but constant using. It'll hurt a little at first, but after some point, more resting won't get it further.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ultimately that's what I most agree with. Crossover in the world of Darkness have three kinds of problems: Inconsistent rules, inconsistent perception of current cosmology, and inconsistent assertions on lore. But the last one isn't so much of a problem, only when such assertions can't be ignored. And the fact is that most players put a lot more of weight on those assertions than they actually have. </div> </div> </div>Agree. Honestly, to me, the first is the worst problem. It's just unnecessary headache. Better crossover rules were something I liked a LOT in NWoD and I hope WWP will take real steps toward easier crossover, primarily in rules but in setting too.<br /> <br /> The other two points: I think those are problems more because people are accustomed to settings with clear-cut truths. Also, players who want to assert their line's viewpoint, status quo and so in a crossover, in contrary to the status quo the ST established might be problematic too. That doesn't mean the lines are mutually exclusive in my book, just that you have to be a little flexible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T15:43:30-08:00","id":1036312,"title":"","content":"Yes, and to realize that some minor powers in some gamelines can be devestating in other gamelines. In MtAs, the True Magick (and Devices) of Technomages is considered technology (it is defined as technology by the setting). In WtA, a common level one Gift is Jam Technology. When you do a crossover, a beginning Garou can disable an orbital fortress capable of killing a Methuselah Kindred (though, to be fair, the Methesulah Kindred can potentially punch the same fortress out of orbit).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T15:54:29-08:00","id":1036316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1036312#post1036312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, and to realize that some minor powers in some gamelines can be devestating in other gamelines. In MtAs, the True Magick (and Devices) of Technomages is considered technology (it is defined as technology by the setting). In WtA, a common level one Gift is Jam Technology. When you do a crossover, a beginning Garou can disable an orbital fortress capable of killing a Methuselah Kindred (though, to be fair, the Methesulah Kindred can potentially punch the same fortress out of orbit).</div> </div> </div> </div>Rank Two, but still probably fairly common, since it can cut off pesky internet feeds before video finds its way onto YT as well as keep cars from starting, guns from firing or knives from cutting..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T16:11:12-08:00","id":1036323,"title":"","content":"Or Garou can use Reshape Object (Level Three) to destroy Devices, Fetishs, or Talismans permanently, which will cause Mages to cry. Garou can potentially turn ships into islands or spacecraft into statues with a Manipulation plus Crafts roll (permanently if they get five successes).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T16:20:21-08:00","id":1036328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1036323#post1036323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Garou can potentially turn ships into islands or spacecraft into statues with a Manipulation plus Crafts roll (permanently if they get five successes).</div> </div> </div> </div>Reshape Object only works on once-living materials, so no, that's out of bounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T13:05:46-08:00","id":1036785,"title":"","content":"Well, you can expect the technocrats and many etherites having massive amounts of Primium in their spacecrafts, so it may be difficult to do that, but still... It is indeed a major problem for techies","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T14:20:40-08:00","id":1036830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1036785#post1036785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you can expect the technocrats and many etherites having massive amounts of Primium in their spacecrafts, so it may be difficult to do that, but still... It is indeed a major problem for techies</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably more than be accounted for by any stated logistical base. White Wolf: worse at economics than Old FASA!*<br /> <br /> As far as passive countermagick goes, the math usually works out to the detriment of someone relying on primium, since it rolls a typically tiny dice pool at difficulty 8, whereas Jam Technology is a full Attribute + Ability dice pool with potential buffs at difficulty 4 for keeping microprocessors down. HIT Marks, thus, are easily dispatched in this fashion, and the bigger and badder and more advanced they are, the more likely they are to take a fall for it.<br /> <br /> (Still holding out for a HIT Mark IX vs. Demon of Iron and Violence fight. Pass the popcorn, the cyber-wrestler is fighting a Cyberdemon from the Wicked City!)<br /> <br /> Also, if you are going with the assumption that mages have spaceships, best never let a wererat Plague Lord onto one. Spacecraft, as it turns out, are actually incredibly filthy places and remarkable breeding grounds for microbes. Such a circumstance would be an incredible opportunity for such a Ratkin.<br /> <br /> *Except for Exalted. But then, its first edition was captained by someone with a serious grounding in economics...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T17:46:15-08:00","id":1036942,"title":"","content":"The best advice I've ever had about this is to treat it as conflicting religious origin tales. Every supernatural group has their own stories and beliefs and while there are figures that have lived through those times they are so godlike that consulting them is next to impossible and they are likely to just give you the corporate pitch rather than the real truth. After all they didn't get that old by telling the truth all the time and giving out the secrets of how things came to be and why they are happening like candy. So any community encountering another communities oring tales will instantly say that isn't how it happened at all this is how it really happened. Which in turn leads into conflicts of who has the right story. Which in turn causes the communities to clash as the have been for the last several centuries keeping the young busy with each other and leaving the old ones free to pursue their own goals and interests with that much less interference.<br /> <br /> As I said that is the best answer I've found. It doesn't solve the problem but makes the problem part of the story thus resolving it becomes a possible goal for the group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12894-grasharm","name":"Grasharm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12894_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T21:59:52-08:00","id":1037048,"title":"","content":"Well, it is not like everyone within each splat agrees on the history anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T03:32:12-08:00","id":1037110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1036830#post1036830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably more than be accounted for by any stated logistical base. White Wolf: worse at economics than Old FASA!*</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1036830#post1036830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as passive countermagick goes, the math usually works out to the detriment of someone relying on primium, since it rolls a typically tiny dice pool at difficulty 8, whereas Jam Technology is a full Attribute + Ability dice pool with potential buffs at difficulty 4 for keeping microprocessors down. HIT Marks, thus, are easily dispatched in this fashion, and the bigger and badder and more advanced they are, the more likely they are to take a fall for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's true. Still, they are almost exclusevly Devices (magikal items), so it may be imune to this Gift, or at least resistant. Problem with counter is that those rules weren't meant to be used against others creatures powers, so it will be up to the ST<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1036830#post1036830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, if you are going with the assumption that mages have spaceships,</div> </div> </div> </div>They do<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1036830#post1036830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">best never let a wererat Plague Lord onto one. Spacecraft, as it turns out, are actually incredibly filthy places and remarkable breeding grounds for microbes. Such a circumstance would be an incredible opportunity for such a Ratkin..</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, its not like the etherite and technos would have a fleet of thousands of those, it would be more like a few dozens each at best, so they would be extremely valued and kept, no dirty allowed<br /> <br /> But, since White Wolf depicts spacial battles of those things on a regular base, all bets are off, so it would be feasible for such big fleets to not be so well maintened (which brings the question: we know that Earth has about 6000 &quot;Mages&quot;... But how many Masters are needed to build and MANTAIN a fleet of space vessels? When I picture things like that, I cannot help but think that the Umbra must have AT LEAST hundreds of thousands of Mages to adhere to those absurd notions... Indeed, no notion of economics whatsoever)<br /> <br /> But I liked that idea of &quot;ratkin infestation&quot;... That's a really cool stuff, it could indeed become a major concern on such a higly inflationated scenario (well, according to RAW, the manufacture of one single of those things would require a lot of time from several Masters, dozens or even hundreds of mages, thousands of sleepers, a ludicruous amount of ether energy and Tass and a lot of time... Still, they say that those guys are shooting each other no stop on the moons of Jupiter... So...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T08:46:07-08:00","id":1037238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1037110#post1037110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, that's true. Still, they are almost exclusevly Devices (magikal items), so it may be imune to this Gift, or at least resistant. Problem with counter is that those rules weren't meant to be used against others creatures powers, so it will be up to the ST</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm reminded of another conversation some time ago about paradigm. As it goes, if the Technocracy and like minds build everything according to technological principles, it doesn't really matter if they're &quot;enlightened&quot; or not, they're still technology by the figuring of other games. Book of the Weaver was chock full of Devices, all without magick. Anything about the Technocracy was in an optional section that was too much Mage in a Werewolf book even then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, its not like the etherite and technos would have a fleet of thousands of those, it would be more like a few dozens each at best, so they would be extremely valued and kept, no dirty allowed </div> </div> </div>So they hope. Whenever you introduce humans and their need to shed skin cells, shed hair, pass waste and sweat and exude oils over everything they touch, things become very dirty in short order. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MRQFJgKS8uo\" target=\"_blank\">Those out of the way access panels catching all that crap don't do much to help.</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But, since White Wolf depicts spacial battles of those things on a regular base, all bets are off, so it would be feasible for such big fleets to not be so well maintened (which brings the question: we know that Earth has about 6000 &quot;Mages&quot;... But how many Masters are needed to build and MANTAIN a fleet of space vessels? When I picture things like that, I cannot help but think that the Umbra must have AT LEAST hundreds of thousands of Mages to adhere to those absurd notions... Indeed, no notion of economics whatsoever) </div> </div> </div>Space opera is one genre that doesn't really play nice with occult conspiracies unless the entire setting is actually a space opera, rather than a modern day bleak Earth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I liked that idea of &quot;ratkin infestation&quot;... That's a really cool stuff, it could indeed become a major concern on such a higly inflationated scenario (well, according to RAW, the manufacture of one single of those things would require a lot of time from several Masters, dozens or even hundreds of mages, thousands of sleepers, a ludicruous amount of ether energy and Tass and a lot of time... Still, they say that those guys are shooting each other no stop on the moons of Jupiter... So...) </div> </div> </div>Maybe move those scenarios off to a far future maybe? CoD probably had the right idea to have separate and highly optional plug-ins for introducing different genres and genre material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 01-24-2017, 02:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T10:32:22-08:00","id":1037282,"title":"","content":"The problem is that it is impossible to keep out the Ratkin, they can literally go anywhere. In addition, since Ratkin work for the Wyld, they really hate Technocrats because of the Weaver association. Oh, Munchmausen can potentially have their own spaceships.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T11:21:27-08:00","id":1037308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1037282#post1037282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that it is impossible to keep out the Ratkin, they can literally go anywhere. In addition, since Ratkin work for the Wyld, they really hate Technocrats because of the Weaver association. Oh, Munchmausen can potentially have their own spaceships.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one really works for the Wyld as such, since it's the closest Supernal to being more a force than a being. The Ratkin come close, but that's because they lost a cornerstone of their cultural being in the War of Rage and became unhinged.<br /> <br /> Also, Munchmausen would probably take a balloon. But since they're Umbral natives, it would be in the Aetherial Realm and most mages would miss it. Another group of Aetherial settlers, The Sept of the Stars, however, could likely be total dicks to unprecedented and overly militaristic space emplacements made by VEs and briefly manifest to nudge space junk into the pathways of kill sats and ships. At the speed that most of said space junk orbits, the impact would be tremendous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T11:40:49-08:00","id":1037323,"title":"","content":"Munchmausen are Deep Umbra travelers as well, so it could be either the Aetherial Realm or the Deep Umbra. Any Fera though could potentially just drop junk in front of the orbital path of a satellite. Without orbital velocity, it will start to fall, but it could run into a satellite with the right calculation. <br /> <br /> Fera could also do a 'Thor's Hammer' move, where they just place a properly designed 100 kilogram tungsten coated iron dart in the proper GEO position and let it fall to the Earth. When it hits the Earth 45 minutes later, it spent 2500 seconds accelerating, so it will pack a punch. It makes you wonder if the reason why the Technocrats do not do it is because they do not want to give anyone else any ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T12:32:16-08:00","id":1037362,"title":"","content":"The Technocrat's Labs (and many etherites too) are absolutely clean... More than clean, they are sterilized to the point of obscession. Mostly, at least.<br /> <br /> But that's not hard to get, since the vast majority of their places have constantly renewed Entropy 3 effects to &quot;keep the Weaver&quot; at its most.<br /> <br /> And remember, they are not <i>just humans</i><br /> <br /> About spacial battles... Well, when we start thinking about spacial vampires, werewolves fighting against cyborgs in Alpha Centaur, spacial stations haunted by ghosts, Gandalf-like saying &quot;You shall not pass!&quot; to a Terminator robot or faeries living in medieval castles on the moon next to a supercomputer, maybe that's the moment to say &quot;it's too much&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T15:37:29-08:00","id":1037451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1037362#post1037362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Technocrat's Labs (and many etherites too) are absolutely clean... More than clean, they are sterilized to the point of obscession. Mostly, at least.<br /> <br /> But that's not hard to get, since the vast majority of their places have constantly renewed Entropy 3 effects to &quot;keep the Weaver&quot; at its most.<br /> <br /> And remember, they are not <i>just humans</i></div> </div> </div> </div>They have to use Life to avoid being filthy and dirty and messing up clean room conditions. It's part of the problem with having a character type without a buy-in hook; they have no default change of state from being humans, so the only things they can do are in a generically-defined power set. The other games center on monsters that all do things, whereas with Mage someone tried to cram in &quot;humans with powers!&quot; as a splat and I don't think it really gels very well, because everyone has their overt magical powers and something else..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> About spacial battles... Well, when we start thinking about spacial vampires, werewolves fighting against cyborgs in Alpha Centaur, spacial stations haunted by ghosts, Gandalf-like saying &quot;You shall not pass!&quot; to a Terminator robot or faeries living in medieval castles on the moon next to a supercomputer, maybe that's the moment to say &quot;it's too much&quot; </div> </div> </div>Didn't you just describe at least half of Mage's setup there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T16:22:06-08:00","id":1037464,"title":"","content":"You are forgetting about Changelings using the Green Paths of Balor take Arcadian Battle Cruisers from the Deep Dreaming to the Deep Umbra. When it comes to the Umbra, Changelings can actually be a major threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T16:58:04-08:00","id":1037485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1037464#post1037464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are forgetting about Changelings using the Green Paths of Balor take Arcadian Battle Cruisers from the Deep Dreaming to the Deep Umbra. When it comes to the Umbra, Changelings can actually be a major threat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where was this written?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T17:13:14-08:00","id":1037497,"title":"","content":"It is a joke. However, since Science Fiction is about dreams of the future and the Deep Dreaming contains all dreams, you could probably find a Star Destroyer in the Deep Dreaming. While it would be an epic task to bring it to the Deep Umbra from the Deep Dreaming, it would not be impossible from my reading of Changeling rules. Imagine the reaction of a Void Engineer when a freaking Star Destroyer comes out of 'hyperspace' and engages their ship with its Turbolasers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T17:24:09-08:00","id":1037500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod?p=1037497#post1037497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is a joke. However, since Science Fiction is about dreams of the future and the Deep Dreaming contains all dreams, you could probably find a Star Destroyer in the Deep Dreaming. While it would be an epic task to bring it to the Deep Umbra from the Deep Dreaming, it would not be impossible from my reading of Changeling rules. Imagine the reaction of a Void Engineer when a freaking Star Destroyer comes out of 'hyperspace' and engages their ship with its Turbolasers?</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends. Is it a computer game Star Destroyer, or a movie one? Because the former are daunting, but the latter have <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Vh0l00Y1760\" target=\"_blank\">some aiming</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wHNB8IHfHdU\" target=\"_blank\">issues....</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T18:08:43-08:00","id":1037529,"title":"","content":"I think it would depend on the exact Deep Dreaming Realm the Changelings stole the Star Destroyer from...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}